(- MCBs from 6 Amperes up to 32 Amperes shall be provided as per the single line diagram.) Tj T*
(- All socket outlet circuits shall be protected by 30 mA RCCBs complying with IS 12640 \(Part) Tj T*
(1\).) Tj T*
(- The earthing installation shall comply with IS 3043:1987.) Tj T*
(- The main distribution board shall be earthed through two pipe earth electrodes.) Tj T*
(- Resistance of the earthing system shall be not more than 1 Ohms.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION 7: TESTING, INSPECTION AND CERTIFICATION) Tj T*
(- Testing of concrete for compressive strength shall be done as per IS 516 \(Part 1/Sec 1\):2021.) Tj T*
(The contractor shall furnish manufacturer's test certificates for every lot of cement and) Tj T*
(reinforcement.) Tj T*
(- The contractor shall submit mill test certificates for all structural steel supplied.) Tj T*
(- Testing of wires shall be done as per IS 10810. After completion, the insulation resistance) Tj T*
(and earth continuity of the installation shall be tested as per IS 732.) Tj T*
(- All wires, MCBs and RCCBs supplied shall carry the ISI mark.) Tj T*
(- Before despatch, the Engineer-in-charge will inspect the equipment at the maker's works.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8 DOCUMENTATION, WARRANTY AND TRAINING) Tj T*
(- Detailed shop drawings are to be submitted by the contractor for approval not later than 21) Tj T*
(calendar days after the award of work.) Tj T*
(- On completion the contractor shall hand over three copies of the O&M manuals.) Tj T*
(- The contractor shall guarantee the whole installation for 12 months after handing over) Tj T*
(against faulty design, materials and workmanship. Operation and routine maintenance training) Tj T*
(shall be given by the contractor to the Department's operators.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
